{"name":"Pixel Nature","hex":"#008751","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pixel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of the tiny dots that make up the representation of an image in a computer's memory.","One of the squares that make up a work of pixel art or a zoomed-in image in a computer."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To create computer graphics by editing individual pixels."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pixel"},{"term":"nature","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The way things are, the totality of all things in the physical universe and their order, especially the physical world in contrast to spiritual realms and flora and fauna as distinct from human conventions, art, and technology.","The particular way someone or something is, especially\nThe essential or innate characteristics of a person or thing which will always tend to manifest, especially in contrast to specific contexts, reason, religious duty, upbringing, and personal pretense or effort."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To endow with natural qualities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nature"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pixel","blocks":[{"text":"In digital imaging, a pixel, pel, or picture element is the smallest addressable element of a raster image. In a display device, dot matrix printer, or ASCII art a pixel is the smallest element whose output can generally be controlled independently."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Pixel-example.png/330px-Pixel-example.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pixel","wikidata":"Q355198"},{"title":"Nature","blocks":[{"text":"Nature, in the broadest sense, is the physical world or universe. In this general sense nature refers to the laws, elements and phenomena of the physical world, including life. Although humans are part of nature, human activity or humans as a whole are 